that transition is happening almost a  year since virtual learning began and  because of the covid pandemic the  average child  is reading six months behind where they  should be  but a relatively new program available  to parents across the country is pairing  up reading coaches with kids  to try to get them back on track kirsten  joyce in studio  she's got the details brian the program  called just right reader was started a  year and a half ago  by harvard grad and founder sarah rich  i'm a reading expert i was a principal  for over 15 years and i kept turning  schools and helping kids in other  schools learn to read  and i realized that my own daughter was  having a hard time learning how to read  so  one day i brought home books that were  right at her level from school  and realized that just like if my own  kid was having a really hard time moms  across america and families across  america needed some help too  so she first started the program by  pairing kids up with age-appropriate  books as you heard but when the pandemic  hit she started hiring amazing teachers  to virtually read with the kids  and it's become as you can guess very  popular the reading and writing program  is for pre-k to sixth grade  they're paired up once or twice a week  for up to 30 minutes with a reading  coach there are also group sessions  available  we also have families that are joining a  reading class  because there's something really special  about being in a group of other kids  we never go higher than five kids or six  kids in a class because we really want  that intimate feeling  of kids being able to talk being able to  be heard  and being able to get the instruction  that's just right for them  there are about 100 people teaching  reading right now but sarah hires about  six to ten new teachers a week due to  the demand  and of course the pricing of the program  varies depending if you go once or twice  a week it is a monthly fee
 

